"A food caterer had to whip up gourmet hot dogs for 36 guests. While most folks would stick to just one hotdog, he made enough for half the guests to grab two. But then, 40 guests turned up, and everyone was keen on a second hotdog. How many guests missed out on a second hotdog?","A food caterer was told to prepare gourmet hot dogs for 36 guests. While most people would only eat one hotdog, he prepared enough for half of the guests to be able to have two hotdogs. However, 40 guests showed up, and everyone wanted a second hotdog. How many guests did not get a second hotdog?",26,26,26,26,"- Planned for 36 guests. Enough for half to have two: total hot dogs = 36 (firsts) + 18 (seconds) = 54.
